        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="9682-26a1-65fb-d7b5" name="Brin Milo" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="model">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="3ff9-87b5-182e-ce1c" type="max" />
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="651e-e69c-285e-fe5f" type="min" />
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="a346-a7a2-d0c9-07c5" name="Tanith Pipes" hidden="false">
              <description>The Tanith Pipes act as a Regimental Standard, although it cannot be captured by the enemy. However, if Milo is killed all Tanith troops (including Gaunt) are at -1 Leadership for the rest of the game.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule id="c49c-57c6-430a-2dd6" name="Precognition" hidden="false">
              <description>Milo has a 4+ Invulnerable save, and confers it to Gaunt if he is within 2" of him.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="9ec6-a2ea-709c-c4af" name="Milo" hidden="false" targetId="06ce-0aba-ce45-1e35" type="profile" />
            <infoLink id="e0b8-06e3-2859-f01f" name="Lasgun" hidden="false" targetId="ce92-3ccf-ee54-f6b1" type="profile" />
            <infoLink id="ae02-3e8b-e585-feda" name="Frag Grenades" hidden="false" targetId="9dd4-e950-2419-5934" type="profile" />
            <infoLink id="83db-6fc9-9c4b-47d2" name="Tanith Knife" hidden="false" targetId="36d3-c20f-b78f-7bf9" type="rule" />
            <infoLink id="2ed1-c9c5-67b9-fdc3" name="Camo Cloak" hidden="false" targetId="647d-f731-5d52-f8e4" type="rule" />
          </infoLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="42" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="8725-c8d7-2fc7-ea9d" name="Master Sniper Mad Larkin" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="model">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="cfab-86ac-4363-2362" type="max" />
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="6a4e-bfda-feba-64ed" type="min" />
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="90b2-eb70-d3bf-d8d9" name="Marksman" hidden="false">
              <description>Larkin nominates a model when he is shooting, such as a Sergeant or a Heavy Weapons trooper. This means he gets to choose which model is removed as a casualty, not the enemy. In addition, Larkin can target any model in range and line of sight, regardless of any targeting restrictions. In addition, Larkin may move and fire his weapon.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule id="5b03-a129-2cb5-1469" name="Customised Long-Las" hidden="false">
              <description>Larkin always hits on a 2+ and wounds on a 4+, rerolling any failed rolls to wound. The long-las has a range of 36" and an AP value of 6, but on the roll of a 5+ to hit it ignores all cover and armour saves.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="9ad0-5b5d-d74a-2eca" name="Frag Grenades" hidden="false" targetId="9dd4-e950-2419-5934" type="profile" />
            <infoLink id="7a82-9130-4c98-694a" name="Lasgun" hidden="false" targetId="ce92-3ccf-ee54-f6b1" type="profile" />
            <infoLink id="0d9b-600c-abb3-146d" name="Sniper Rifle" hidden="false" targetId="3825-4a6b-6aaa-8c99" type="profile" />
            <infoLink id="df8e-f041-65d1-1977" name="Camo Cloak" hidden="false" targetId="647d-f731-5d52-f8e4" type="rule" />
            <infoLink id="9987-ff32-48e4-2591" name="Larkin" hidden="false" targetId="b0fb-17ed-3ca8-2609" type="profile" />
          </infoLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="37" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="dc74-dac1-b893-8a01" name="Try Again Bragg" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="model">
          <comment>https://web.archive.org/web/20070124114945/http://uk.games-workshop.com/imperialguard/gaunts-ghosts/</comment>
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="81fd-19f1-eabf-9413" type="max" />
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="70b1-87bb-78c6-c8c8" type="min" />
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="fa77-d54e-069c-23ff" name="Brawn" hidden="false">
              <description>Bragg is almost legendarily strong. He may move and fire with his heavy bolter, although this does nothing for his already shoddy accuracy...</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="bfd1-e833-cb4b-24a9" name="Bragg" hidden="false" targetId="4faf-4c4d-1116-df81" type="profile" />
            <infoLink id="c27d-2f22-bea4-40dc" name="Heavy Bolter" hidden="false" targetId="b9aa-366b-bd62-4692" type="profile" />
            <infoLink id="39c0-f79c-fc78-8c19" name="Frag Grenades" hidden="false" targetId="9dd4-e950-2419-5934" type="profile" />
            <infoLink id="12dc-59a2-acea-b144" name="Camo Cloak" hidden="false" targetId="647d-f731-5d52-f8e4" type="rule" />
          </infoLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="23" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="056b-9185-0c87-2589" name="Major Rawne" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="model">
          <comment>https://web.archive.org/web/20070124114945/http://uk.games-workshop.com/imperialguard/gaunts-ghosts/</comment>
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="e31e-06c8-0716-19de" type="max" />
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="0fd6-df01-3ab3-9955" type="min" />
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="4786-6965-8833-5e8a" name="Grudge" hidden="false">
              <description>At the start of every Imperial Guard Assault phase, if the squad ever comprises of only Gaunt and Major Rawne and they are not already in close combat, Rawne must pass a Leadership test or will attack Gaunt as if he were an enemy model until one of them is removed as a casualty. The survivor may act normally from that point onward.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="49d1-b817-6669-8dea" name="Rawne" hidden="false" targetId="3bc6-3751-dde1-a816" type="profile" />
            <infoLink id="79ab-0e2c-7543-b098" name="Lasgun" hidden="false" targetId="ce92-3ccf-ee54-f6b1" type="profile" />
            <infoLink id="dc78-c9d9-2f4e-b307" name="Frag Grenades" hidden="false" targetId="9dd4-e950-2419-5934" type="profile" />
            <infoLink id="529f-3a54-436a-4579" name="Demolition Charge" hidden="false" targetId="60f0-36e3-b539-71ac" type="profile" />
            <infoLink id="5eef-6dd0-d503-65fa" name="Camo Cloak" hidden="false" targetId="647d-f731-5d52-f8e4" type="rule" />
          </infoLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="23" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="8639-086e-c5d2-314e" name="Sergeant Mkoll" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="model">
          <comment>https://web.archive.org/web/20070124114945/http://uk.games-workshop.com/imperialguard/gaunts-ghosts/</comment>
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="24be-90dc-75d2-a582" type="max" />
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="21a9-c9d2-b361-c296" type="min" />
          </constraints>
          <rules>
            <rule id="bf91-be22-6b9e-3852" name="Peerless Scout" hidden="false">
              <description>Mkoll may be detached from Gaunt's retinue to lead a squad of Tanith troops (Tanith Hardened Veterans or Tanith Infantry). Mkoll and any unit he leads may re-roll any failed cover saves; the second result must be applied. They may deploy in Ambush (as detailed on page 20 of Codex Catachans), or as normal Infiltrators if the controlling player wishes and if the Infiltrators special rule is being used. If Mkoll is spotted by or attacks a Sentry model, the alarm is only raised on the D6 roll of a 6. Mkoll doubles his Initiative when in combat with Sentries.</description>
            </rule>
            <rule id="07d9-cd59-8075-bf82" name="Acute Perception" hidden="false">
              <description>Mkoll is adept at picking out anomalies in the landscape and can scan an area for Ambushes, Booby Traps and Lictors as if he was equipped with an Auspex (see pages 20/21 of Codex: Catachans)</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <infoLinks>
            <infoLink id="b304-8b15-61a7-ea8d" name="Lasgun" hidden="false" targetId="ce92-3ccf-ee54-f6b1" type="profile" />
            <infoLink id="521d-f1d6-0c22-65b9" name="Frag Grenades" hidden="false" targetId="9dd4-e950-2419-5934" type="profile" />
            <infoLink id="5dfd-4139-0870-9a7e" name="Camo Cloak" hidden="false" targetId="647d-f731-5d52-f8e4" type="rule" />
          </infoLinks>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="23" />
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="0" />
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
